{title: As a Deer Longs}
{subtitle: Psalms 42:2–6}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] |
| [Bb] | [Gm7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm7]I remember Sun[Fsus4]day mornings and [F]the singing [Bb]in the hall
How I walked among [Gm7]the people and I felt you [Cm7]over all
Now the house is ve[Fsus4]ry quiet and the [F]nights are very [Bb]long
And I search for you [Gm7]in silence where [Eb]I used to find a song
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]As a deer longs [Gm7]for streams of water
[Bb/D]So my soul longs for you, [Eb]O God
My soul [F]thirsts for God, [Bb]for [Gm7]the living God
When shall [Eb]I come and [Bb]appear before God's face
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My [F]tears have been [Gm7]my food day and night
And still [Eb]the voices ask me [Bb]where you are
I pour [F]my heart out on the kitchen floor
I hold [Bb]on to the memory [Gm7]of the [Eb]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
As a deer longs for [F]streams of wa[Gm7]ter
So my soul longs [Bbmaj7/D]for you, O God
My soul [Eb]thirsts for God, for [F]the living [Bb]God
[Eb]When shall I come and ap[F]pear be[Bb]fore God's face
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F/A]Why are you cast [Gm7]down, my soul
[Eb]And why do you groan within me
Hope in [F]God, for I [Bb]will praise him a[Gm7]gain
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
As a [Eb]deer longs for streams of wa[F]ter
So my [Gm7]soul longs for you, O [Bbmaj7/D][Eb]God
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [F] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7/D] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |
